WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:04.974
Two people with fatty liver disease can have
very different outcomes.

2
00:00:05.294 --> 00:00:10.344
Why does one develop liver scarring, or even
cancer, while the other remains stable?

3
00:00:11.183 --> 00:00:15.790
At Taipei Medical University, our lab looks for
clues in human DNA.

4
00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:21.403
We compare people at different stages of
disease to find genetic variants linked to
risk.

5
00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:27.473
In the blood, we track molecules ranging from
lipids and amino acids to lactate.

6
00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:32.543
We follow their levels over time to see which
changes accompany disease progression.

7
00:00:33.392 --> 00:00:35.579
Liver tissue gives us a closer look.

8
00:00:35.899 --> 00:00:42.712
We use artificial intelligence to identify fat
droplets and clusters of inflammatory cells on
a slide.

9
00:00:43.558 --> 00:00:47.883
Together, these clues point us toward
biological pathways worth testing.

10
00:00:48.203 --> 00:00:54.260
Then we use experimental models to ask whether
those pathways influence how the disease
progresses.
